the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base ex11_maternity_alternatives includes these resources:
    deontic.

the templates are:
    *an income* is earned in *a year*.
    the maternity benefit is *an amount* in *a year*.
    *an income* is reported in *a year*.
    *a number* is 80 percent of five twelfths of *an income*.
    the interpretation adopted is *an interpretation*.

the knowledge base ex11_maternity_alternatives includes:

the text of the source document is at "sources/ex11-maternity_alternatives-normal.lrml".

ref1 is published at "ECLI:IT:PCBO:1996:18".

ref2 is published at "http://www.normattiva.it/uri-res/N2Ls?urn:nir:stato:decreto.legge:1990-12-11;379~art1".

ex_ref1 is published at "http://example.org#ref1".

% authority pc: http://example.org/authority#prosecutorOffice
% authority abit: http://example.org/authority#associationBar-Italy
% jurisdiction it: http://example.org/jurisdiction#italy
rule literal with provenance ex_ref1:
a party is obliged that the maternity benefit is an amount in a year Y if
    a year N = Y - 2
    and an income is earned in N
    and a year M = Y - 2
    and the income is reported in M
    and the interpretation adopted is literal
    and the income is 80 percent of five twelfths of the amount.

% If income is earned in some year, then it is reported in the following year.
rule tax1:
an income is reported in a year Y if
    the income is earned in a year N
    and Y = N + 1.

% If income is reported in some year, then it was earned in the previous year.
rule tax2:
an income is earned in a year Y if
    the income is reported in a year N
    and Y = N - 1.

query earned is:
    which income is earned in which year.

query obligations is:
    which party is obliged that which sentence.

query reported is:
    which income is reported in which year.

query violated_obligations is:
    the obligation of which party that which sentence is violated.

query breaches is:
    which party is in breach.

